      evidence: line-length CV 0.081 < 0.0845 (human 5th percentile, lyric profile, evaluated at N=69 tokens from -0.0955481 +0.059242·ln N -0.00394609·(ln N)^2). NOT slop evidence: this check was built expecting metronomic lines to be a generated-text tell and the measurement came out BACKWARDS — Shakespeare is more uniform than the model. NO generated class exists at this length, so there is no AUC and no separation claim; the evidence is a false-positive rate of 5.11% on HELD-OUT human song (5th-95th percentile of seeds 4.11-6.36%). It says how often this fires on a human songwriter, not whether it catches a machine. In a fixed form uniformity is the form. Retained only as 'outside the human range', and meaningful, if at all, in free verse

